From 0e97992e1a66f8d363634540c21218dfad262d1f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Will Norris <will@biohack.net>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:45:39 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 04/14] [MOS] Extract far data addressing and bounded runtime
 indexing

Extract the p2:32 data-pointer model, Imag32 quads, default register ABI,
far data legalization and selection, allocation support, and bounded byte
index folding from downstream 0001/0002. Keep upstream vector rules,
wide-constant guards, pointer increment behavior, and native DWARF numbers.
Imag32 quads have no assigned DWARF number.

Exclude packed storage, far function calls, experimental calling
conventions, near no-wrap recovery, and SNES configurations. Two near
store assertions now describe the fallback used without no-wrap recovery;
their far indexing checks remain.

The compiler/ABI prerequisites are a review scaffold. ABI acceptance,
argument exhaustion, memory-intrinsic lengths above 65535, and debugger
integration require their own review. This is not an upstream submission.
Existing implementation provenance remains in the source patches and
investigations at wbniv/llvm-mos-65816 c3a53aecbc48.

Validation with the native and assembler prerequisites: assertions build;
MOS CodeGen and MC suites, 150 passed and one unsupported.

Rebase preparation: OpenAI Codex CLI 0.157.1 (session source vscode),
model gpt-6-astra, xhigh reasoning effort; verified session
01a0e67f-298f-7a21-80af-06f867085f84.
